# A style guide whose tags name what exists

The legend above the first section describes the forms with placeholders, such as
`[tidy:<rule-id>]`, and is not checked.

## Rules

- A rule and a ban of the registry. `[tidy:line-length]` `[tidy:direct-libm]`
- A lint that is switched on, and one of the pedantic group. `[clippy:unwrap_used]`
  `[clippy:pedantic]`
- A compiler lint that is switched on. `[rustc:missing_docs]`
- A lint of the project library that is declared. `[dylint:nami_recursion]`
- A mechanism that is planned, next to judgement. `[planned:glossary]` `[review]`
- The plain mechanisms. `[compiler]` `[fmt]` `[deny]`
- Code in backticks is not a tag: `[f64; NVAR]` states and `field[CellIndex]` gathers.

```rust
// A `[tidy]` inside a code block is not a tag either.
```
